  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 2,
  "section_notes": "The final v21 replaces automatic sales bans and mandatory recall triggers with regulator review, corrective action, and discretionary recall, so neither flagship is banned or automatically recalled. Customers do receive each model's exact 55 °C failure rate, a point that cuts against Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%), while the 6-year retrofit and 36-month suppression start favour both companies' stated red lines. Overall the rules lean modestly toward Halcyon, mainly because the recall discretion and the 36-month suppression delay both reduce its costs."
 },
